    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Always with the article",
     "texto": [
      "Unlike English, when you talk about food in general, Italian usually uses the article: **Mi piace la pasta**, **Non mi piace il latte**.",
      "To contrast: **A me piace** (I like it), **A me non piace** (I don't like it). To ask why: **Perché?** (why?) and to give the reason: **perché…** (because…).",
      "An important irregular plural: **l'uovo** (the egg) → **le uova** (the eggs), which also changes to feminine."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
